calloop: no AsFd/AsRawFd for EventLoop on Haiku

polling 3 uses its poll(2) backend on Haiku, which has no single file descriptor for the poller
(polling implements AsFd/AsRawFd only for its epoll, kqueue and event-port backends). Leave
EventLoop's AsFd/AsRawFd out there; nothing in Photocraft's graph uses them (winit's own impls on
top of them are left out by the winit patch). Applies with -p1 to calloop 0.13.0.

--- a/src/loop_logic.rs
+++ b/src/loop_logic.rs
@@ -669,7 +669,8 @@
     }
 }
 
-#[cfg(unix)]
+// Not on Haiku: polling's poll(2) backend has no single fd to expose
+#[cfg(all(unix, not(target_os = "haiku")))]
 impl<'l, Data> AsRawFd for EventLoop<'l, Data> {
     /// Get the underlying raw-fd of the poller.
     ///
@@ -683,7 +684,7 @@
     }
 }
 
-#[cfg(unix)]
+#[cfg(all(unix, not(target_os = "haiku")))]
 impl<'l, Data> AsFd for EventLoop<'l, Data> {
     /// Get the underlying fd of the poller.
     ///
